# Static UI text (`UiText`)

All **user-visible static strings** come from `src/constants/uiText` via `UiText`.

## Source of truth

| Concern | Location |
|---------|----------|
| Labels, buttons, placeholders, aria-labels, empty states, toasts, page body copy | `src/constants/uiText/*` → `UiText` |
| Routes / path helpers | `src/lib/paths.ts` |
| Nav/footer **structure** (href wiring) | `src/config/site.ts` — **labels** from `UiText` |
| Brand **name** / locale / icon paths | `src/config/site.ts` — tagline/description from `UiText.brand` when applicable |
| SEO builders | `src/lib/metadata.ts` (compose `UiText` + `site`) |

## Rules

- Do **not** hardcode UI copy in JSX/TSX (buttons, nav labels, headings, body paragraphs, hints, `aria-label`, placeholders, breadcrumbs).
- Import: `import { UiText, formatUiText } from "@/constants/uiText"`.
- Templates use `{name}` / `{tagline}` — resolve with `formatUiText(template, { name: site.name })`.
- Reuse `UiText.actions.*` / `UiText.common.*` — do not redefine shared verbs in feature modules.
- Add keys to the right module file; register new modules in `index.ts`.
- Keep API/enum **values** separate from **display** labels.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<button aria-label="Search">Search</button>

// ✅ GOOD
<button aria-label={UiText.navigation.search}>
  {UiText.actions.search}
</button>
```

```ts
// ✅ site.ts — structure + UiText labels
{ label: UiText.navigation.about, href: paths.about }
```

## Exclude

Routes, permission keys, CSS class names, env vars, and user-entered / API-driven content.
